From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:46:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 123/148] fix(refinery): port upstream's #245 merge lane and
 task-artifact cleanup into merge-push.sh (gcp-fooz4)

merge-push.sh (gcp-l8td.5/.6) is the merge-push step's lane moved out of the
formula, and gcp-l8td.6 retired the formula copy. Upstream 520e95cb rewrote
that lane (f709abe5 #245, the task-artifact lifecycle, #374), so after the
BASELINE upgrade the script still ran the pre-#245 lane. Port the new lane:

- mr, approval off: record the pending PR with `gc gastown pr-merge-reconcile
  record` (bead BLOCKED until a later patrol verifies the merge) and mail the
  mayor, instead of closing at publication. Breadcrumbs move into the
  approval-on lane, which still lands the approved head itself.
- lookup_pr_info reads headRefOid (gh and REST); the PR head must equal the
  validated temp before anything is recorded.
- direct, approved mr, and already-merged closes keep origin/$BRANCH (the
  artifact's recovery copy; delete_merged_branches is deprecated) and run
  `gc gastown task-artifact-cleanup "$WORK"` after the verified close.
- force-with-lease failure drops temp and re-enters the rebase step's
  ancestry decision on the next patrol; never an in-place rebase (#374).
- PR body says "Based on", not "Rebased on".

Tests follow the lane: merge-lanes/merge-batch stubs model the two pack
commands, mr cases expect the pending record, the direct cleanup case expects
the source branch kept; upstream's test_pr_merge_reconcile and rebase-guard
legs 9/10 read the publication-path and lease-recovery contract from the
script; inference-gate script pins follow.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
